M cascade kickoff. Unblocked when 024B-extras merges.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:37:The script enforces the spec from plan-doc §2 invariant 2. Regex (Python re):\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:45:- ✅ ex1: STATUS.md bullet-bold form `- **TF-024X-renovate-jrnb2024-pim** (open): Renovate disabled on PIM; operator-bumped @abc123 at 024C; track until adopter enables Renovate cohort.`\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:56:- [ ] CI enforcement script implements all 5 cascade-status check-paths (4 enforcement + `not applicable`).\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:58:- [ ] No --restore-mode content in any file (extras carve-out clean).\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:60:- [ ] No ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass content (extras carve-out clean).\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:61:- [ ] D-044 row scoped to core deliverables.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:68:None for 024B-core. Cascade-start announcement files at 024C kickoff (per plan-doc §5.5).\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:72:[none new since 2026-05-04 (024A close)] — slice 024B-core is internal scaffolding; no FLA implications.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:76:Same deviation as parent 024B: direct `codex exec` / `claude -p` (kernel hook lives in ACC, not SCP; per-repo install pattern is FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 — still open). Compensating manual steps (scope check + verify-cmds + audit log) apply to this slice as well.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:83:| 1 | Codex executor: surgical clean of test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh (remove --restore tests); D-044 row; STATUS.md entry; verify scaffolder + check-invocation-log-entry.sh have no extras coupling | Codex T3 | ~30 min |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:89:Target: 024B-core merged within ~2–3 hours (vs 4 days + $50 reviewer cost on the original 024B).\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:93:D-044 stays reserved for this slice (core). Codex must NOT assign D-044 to anything else. 024B-extras may file sibling D-NNN at extras-authoring time.\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:3:**Last Updated:** 2026-05-03 (D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A; estate cascade)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:29:> **D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 024A):**\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:30:> D-044 is reserved for WP-SCP-024 slice 024B (`scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:33:> --restore` rollback mode). D-045 is reserved for slice 024C (estate\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:43:> assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:70:| D-023 | 2026-04-21 | Reject multi-agent free-form chat-forum pattern as the agent-coordination venue; adopt structured proposal queue (`docs/reviews/proposals/PROP-NNN.md` + MCP `propose()` tool — initial stub in WP-SCP-021 slice 021E; full adjudication workflow in `WP-SCP-022-proposal-queue`, separately tracked per `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §12). Agents never free-form chat with each other; they read SCP's decision records and call SCP's MCP tools | ACCEPTED | Du et al. (ICML 2024, `arxiv 2305.14325`) show multi-agent debate converges to consensus fast including when the consensus is wrong; Anthropic's multi-agent research post reports ~15× token cost with compounding coordination errors; human-on-the-loop literature converges on moderator-as-bottleneck past a few decisions/hour. Proposal-queue pattern scales because the human is on the loop, not in it. Full rationale body in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §10 (decision originator) and `docs/plans/WP-SCP-021-scp-as-mcp-server.md` §10 (`propose()` stub design). Note 2026-04-28: original D-023 forward-referenced \"WP-SCP-022 plan when that WP opens\"; WP-SCP-022 v0.2 is the implementation programme plan, not the proposal-queue WP — the rationale-body expansion lives in the parent plans named here, and the adjudication WP is renamed `WP-SCP-022-proposal-queue` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:88:| D-041 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B (this PR). The schema defines aggregated per-rule counts (raw_findings, denies, waived, rule_config_disabled), waivers aggregate (active_count, by_rule_id, expiring_within_30d), rule-config aggregate (disabled_rules, expiring_within_30d), repo / ref / commit / scp_version / RFC3339 emitted_at, and a verdict (allow/deny/warn). The schema EXPLICITLY DOES NOT include waiver content (`reason`, `approved_by`, `waiver_id` strings) — invariant 2 of WP-SCP-023 plan-doc binds this. The reusable workflow gains a `scorecard-emit: bool` `workflow_call` input (default false) so existing adopters see no behaviour change; opt-in adopters set `with: scorecard-emit: true`. Schema versioning: MAJOR-pinned per `policies/VERSIONING.md` D-036 + WP-SCP-023 plan-doc §10 Q1 — aggregator drops emits with unknown `schema_version`. Verification: GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation (OIDC-based) via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0` (SHA `a2bbfa25...`) at emit time; aggregator verifies via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow` (per D-042 to be filed at slice 023C). v1.2.0 cut on this slice's merge per VERSIONING.md MINOR category | ACCEPTED | This is the first slice of WP-SCP-023's implementation chain (023A plan-doc landed at PR #97, commit `7075234`, 2026-05-03 R4 fixpoint). The data shape was specified at plan-doc level; this slice ratifies it as code surface. Default-false on the workflow input is the load-bearing safety property: existing adopters cannot have new behaviour spring on them; opt-in is explicit per invariant 4. The waiver-content exclusion (invariant 2) is enforced by the schema's `additionalProperties: false` constraint on every level + the explicit field enumeration. The MAJOR-pinning posture means schema breakage requires v2.0.0 + adopter migration; v0.1 prefix on `schema_version` reflects the freedom to amend until first adopter opts in. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:89:| D-042 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard aggregator pipeline trust model per WP-SCP-023 023C (this PR). Mechanism: per-emit verification via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow <expected_workflow_ref>` (the GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation OIDC pattern, mandatory per the D-042 reservation note above + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure); index trust rooted in git's required-signed-commits (slice 020J) + `output/scorecards/** @jrnb2024` CODEOWNERS coverage (slice 023A) + branch protection on main (slice 020D2), NOT a separate Ed25519 key layer. The aggregator runs as `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` on a weekly cron (Monday 06:00 UTC) + `workflow_dispatch`; two-job structure (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped via job-level permissions, mirroring the 023B `attest-scorecard` job split); reads `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` (CODEOWNERS-protected at `docs/scorecards/**`), pulls each adopter's latest green policy-check run's `scorecard-emit.json` artifact, verifies attestation, schema-validates emit, aggregates into `output/scorecards/index.json` (schema: `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`), and opens a PR for operator review. Failure modes (verification_failure / unreachable / no_emit) record loudly per-adopter — never silently dropped. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema `additionalProperties: false` at every level). Internal-only workflow per `policies/VERSIONING.md` §\"Scope\" (mirrors 020N conflict-gate.yml posture); no semver bump. Verifies WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 6 (\"Aggregator output is Ed25519-signed\") in spirit — Sigstore/Fulcio uses Ed25519 under the hood, managed by GitHub rather than by an SCP-side private key, eliminating the private-key-distribution surface | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 (per-emit data shape + opt-in model) — D-041 ratified the EMITTER side of the trust model; D-042 ratifies the AGGREGATOR / VERIFIER side. The mandatory `--signer-workflow` constraint was already pre-committed at the D-042 reservation note above (closes 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001) — this slice ratifies it as workflow code. The Ed25519-via-Sigstore framing eliminates the chicken-and-egg of \"where does the SCP private key live and how does the aggregator hold it without exposing adopters\" — GitHub manages the keys via OIDC + Sigstore. The two-job permission split (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped) is identical to 023B's `policy-check` + `attest-scorecard` split (closes the analogous threat surface where workflow-level write permissions could be exploited by a compromised aggregate-side step). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-042 reservation + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:90:| D-043 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report (`docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`) + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D (this PR). Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` produces deterministic golden-file-tested output reading `output/scorecards/index.json`; aggregator workflow `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` extended in the commit job to invoke the generator + add the rendered markdown to the operator-review PR alongside the index. MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` (registered in `src/standards_control_plane/mcp_server/tools.py`): read-only contract per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 5; request shape `{repo_filter?, since_emitted_at?}`; response shape excludes waiver content (`reason` / `approved_by` / `waiver_id` — invariant 2) by Pydantic model construction (extra=forbid + explicit field whitelist). The MCP method reads `output/scorecards/index.json` from the SCP repo working copy at call time; staleness is observable via the response's `aggregated_at` field. ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by Pydantic models + schema + dedicated pytest scans on both markdown + MCP responses) | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 + D-042 — D-043 ratifies the CONSUMER side: markdown for operators/auditors, MCP for agents/tooling. Read-only contract + Pydantic-enforced field whitelist + golden-file pytest together preserve invariant 2 across both surfaces. The MCP method does NOT introduce a new authentication primitive — it rides on WP-SCP-021's existing Ed25519 receipt mechanism (consult-class semantics). The markdown report is informational and CODEOWNERS-protected via `docs/scorecards/** @jrnb2024`; operators can hand-edit before merging the aggregator PR if needed (regenerator overwrites on next run). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the MCP server runs at acc.brokapps.ai; if down, agents lose `consult_scorecard` access but the markdown report + git index remain consultable. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md:1:# Scope correction — WP-SCP-024 024B split into 024B-core + 024B-extras\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md:4:**Operator decision:** split slice 024B into two slices.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md:8:WP-SCP-024 slice 024B as originally scoped accumulated 7 fix-rounds + 7 adversarial-review rounds against a single branch. Trajectory:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md:12:| R1 | 2 | 9 | Worked-example ma